# Tabletop UI

Tabletop is the **default** production skin. Classic is rollback-only.

Full visual authority order and anatomy details: `docs/DESIGN_AUTHORITY.md`.

## Isolation

- Import only `./tabletop.css` from the Tabletop skin entry
- Never import Classic components, helpers, or Classic stylesheets into the active Tabletop graph
- Registry may register Classic via `./classic/skin` (components only); Classic CSS lives under `./classic/styles` and must not load while `ACTIVE_SKIN_ID` is `tabletop`
- Every rule scoped under `.tabletop-skin` / `[data-skin="tabletop"]`
- No global generic selectors (`.box`, `.table`, `.dealer`, `.felt` without skin scope)
- No `!important` cascade fixes for architectural conflicts
- Remove obsolete selectors instead of layering overrides

## Visual authority

1. Original approved PNGs under `design/reference/classic/approved/`
2. Product phase/control/role contracts
3. Tabletop implementation
4. HTML prototype as secondary token colour reference only
5. Historical/implementation screenshots are never design authority

## Composition contract

- Phone composition: `100dvh`, max width ~480px, **no document scroll**
- Minimum interactive target 44×44px
- `BlackjackTableSurface` owns Blackjack table geometry: emerald cloth + fabric texture + vignette, curved double gold rail, insurance/BJ rule arcs (CSS/SVG), embroidered table name, Dealer position, player layer
- Felt/table is the permanent base; overlays never replace it with an admin panel
- PhaseDisplay: title on line 1, instruction on line 2 — never side-by-side; reserve stable height
- Setup joined Players use compact `JoinedPlayerMark` (`PLAYER JOINED`) — never READY / MAIN BET / spreadsheet rows
- Betting / Playing / Insurance use shared `BlackjackBoxStage` physical positions for Dealer and Player
- Full-width `DealerLedgerRow` bars are **Payout only**
- Table name printed on felt: complete name visible, `clamp()` sizing, up to two centred lines, no ellipsis on ordinary names
- Dealer and Player devices are two viewpoints onto the same physical table
- Stable anatomy across phase transitions: same felt/rail/Dealer/box-stage Y; phases change labels, values, and legal controls
- `prefers-reduced-motion` must not rely on motion for meaning
- One canonical visible component per screen/role; adapters only when they mount that component
- One stylesheet (`tabletop.css`) owns Blackjack table geometry; no Classic CSS in the active bundle

## Rejected presentation (do not restore)

CSS diamond-hatch wallpaper felt, plain single-colour felt gradient as finished anatomy, decorative 2px ellipse rail as finished anatomy, dashed-circle chips, kidney/spatial Dealer plaques, `data-arc` / `data-dealer-positions` as visual contracts, duplicated Dealer identity in header and felt, PhaseZero admin ledger as a second Dealer screen path, padded “Open seat” / minimum-row placeholders, 2×2 Blackjack payout button grids, separate `TableCloth` bottom plaque, nested felt panels, giant bordered Player-list spreadsheet, full-width ledger bars outside Payout, Setup `READY` rows, side-by-side phase title+instruction, ellipsised table names.

## Tests

Behavioural tests protect commands, legal actions, balances, roles, overflow, and accessibility. They must **not** freeze rejected DOM/class names or Classic-only selectors as Tabletop requirements.
